{
 "id": "dungeon-root-v1",
 "description": "Walkable ROOT INTERIOR kit \u2014 the missing tileset behind the province's signature dungeon family (catalogue.py INTERIOR_FAMILIES `root-cavern` and `hist-sanctum`, plus the `root-hollow-gallery` and `wild-rootworm-burrow` place types, whose assetPlans previously pointed at TREE meshes that cannot make a walkable interior \u2014 see docs/research/place-asset-deliverability-audit.md \u00a73/\u00a75.2). Pure packaging: every piece already existed in the vault, unkitted. Three authored modular sets are packaged SEPARATELY, each in its own snap logic (see snapLogic) \u2014 they are never interpenetrated piece-for-piece: (1) BM&V `philscaves`, a complete Morrowind-style modular cave tileset (small corridors/halls/ramp/exits plus the larger `srooms` room-and-corridor family and two cave shells) \u2014 the walkable SHELL, read as root-wall via its own texture set; (2) BM&V `citebosmer` trunk-house INTERIOR modules \u2014 the inside-a-trunk storeys, walls, windows, doors and trapdoor stairs that make a hollow living root; (3) BM&V `telvanni` root/interior pieces (`tel_ext_root_01/02`, `tel_root_03`, connector, ramp, stairs, gourd-house shell) \u2014 organic connective tissue between the two. Dressed with HTBM Cipactli's Hist root masses (`histroots01-06`, `histramp`, `treeroots`, `treeroottrap`, corrupted taproots) and Mud Mother Grove's Argonian ritual lights, shell floor, Sithis shrine and Hist mist for the hist-sanctum centre. NOT tropicalised: nothing here is vanilla-backed, so the overlay would be a no-op. TEXTURE NOTE: the BM&V Telvanni pieces UV Dragonborn's `textures/dlc02/architecture/telvannitower/*` paths and the vault holds NO Skyrim DLC, so they exported grey. `textureAliases` redirects all twelve DLC paths (plus two Earrindo and two Stroti wood paths BM&V also fails to ship) to BM&V's OWN Bosmer bark `eressea/architecture/citesylvestrepactevert/bark0143` \u2014 which is exactly the 'retexture the Telvanni silhouette to root' the audit asks for, done as a build-config alias rather than a new texture. Same mechanism as settlement-stilt-v1's stockade redirect.",
