 "snapLogic": {
  "philscaves": "Its own Morrowind-derived modular cave grid. Pieces are authored around a shared corridor cross-section and butt END-TO-END at their open faces with no offset; the origin sits at the piece's entry face. `small/cor01-04` are the turn set, `small/hall01-05` the straights, `small/ram01` the vertical change, `small/exit01-02` and `small/doorcaveb` the terminators, `small/cap` seals a stub. The `srooms` family is a second, larger tier with the same convention: `connect` is the adapter between a `room0x` chamber and a `cor0x` run, `corc0x` are its corners, `mid0x` the extensions, `wall0x` the blanking faces. Mix tiers only through `srooms/connect`. `cave2`/`cave3` are one-piece shells used as a terminal chamber, not as modules.",
  "citebosmer-interiors": "The Bosmer tree-city set's own storey grid. Names encode the storey: `rc` = ground storey, `et` = upper storey, `ss` = basement. A dwelling is one `...int<storey>001` floor shell with `intwall<storey>00x` panels and `intwindow<storey>00x` inserts substituted around its perimeter, `intdoor<storey>01` at the entry, and storeys stacked vertically and joined by the `gland` trapdoor family (`inttraprcup001`/`inttraprcdn001`/`inttrapetdn001`/`inttrapssup001` \u2014 up/down at ground, down from upper, up from basement). `90v` suffixes are the 90-degree rotated variants authored to close a corner; `15v`/`45v` on the champ walls are the wall's authored tilt for the tapering trunk, so a champ shell must use one tilt family consistently.",
  "telvanni": "Free-form organic connectors, not a grid. `tel_int_connector_01` is the authored joint between two pod/root volumes; `tel_ext_root_01/02` and `tel_root_03` are placed by hand against a shell mouth. Use them to hide the seam where philscaves meets a citebosmer trunk interior.",
  "htbm-roots": "Dressing statics with no connectors \u2014 `histroots01-06` are hand-placed root masses, `histramp` is the one traversable piece and is authored to lie on the ground plane as a walk-up.",
  "unitScale": "Bethesda units; the pipeline converts at 0.0142240 m/unit. Measured extents per piece are in the built manifest tooling/asset-pipeline/output/kits/dungeon-root-v1.kit.json."
 },
